hadiths[60]{hadithnumber,text}:
"571","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says, ""Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting; it is especially for Me, and I alone will reward it. And fasting is a shield (from sins)."" Then, when any of you is fasting, he should neither utter foul words nor raise his voice. If someone abuses him or tries to fight with him, he should say, 'I am fasting.' By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), surely the smell from the mouth of a fasting person is more beloved to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the fragrance of musk. And the fasting person has two joys with which he rejoices: one when he breaks his fast, and the other when he meets his Lord due to his fasting."
"572","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained tightly."
"573","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not fast one or two days before Ramadan, except for a person who used to fast on a particular (fixed) day, and that day coincides (with these days), then he may fast on his fixed day. (For example, if he used to fast on Thursday and Friday, and the 29th or 30th of Sha’ban falls on those days, then he may fast.)"
"574","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the moon and said: When you see the moon, then fast. And when you see it (again), then break your fast. But if clouds come, then complete thirty days of fasting (and then celebrate Eid)."
"575","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath that he would not go to his wives for a month. (But) when twenty-nine (29) days had passed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his wives in the morning or evening. He was told, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you had taken an oath that you would not come to us for a month.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, “A month can also be of twenty-nine days.”"
"576","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: We are an unlettered nation; we neither write nor calculate. The month is like this, like this, and like this. And the third time, he folded his thumb. And the month is like this, like this, and like this. That is, it completes thirty days."
"577","Sayyiduna Abu’l-Bakhtari (may Allah have mercy on him) says: We set out for ‘Umrah, and when we reached the middle of (the place) Nakhlah, everyone began to look at the moon. Some, after seeing it, said that it was a three-night-old moon (i.e., because of its size), and some said it was two nights old. Then we met Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and mentioned to him that we had seen the moon, and some said it was three nights old and some said two nights old. Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) then asked: On which night did you see it? We replied: On such-and-such night. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said that Allah Almighty has made it appear larger for sighting. It was of the same night as the night you saw it."
"578","Kuraib reports that Lady Umm Fadl bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) sent him to (the land of) Syria to Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: I went to Syria and completed his task, and I saw the crescent of Ramadan on the night of Friday (i.e., Thursday evening). Then, at the end of the month, I came to Madinah. Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) asked me and mentioned the crescent, asking: When did you see it? I said: On the night of Friday. He asked: Did you see it yourself? I said: Yes, and the people also saw it and fasted, and Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and the people also fasted. Then Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: But we saw it on the night of Saturday, so we will complete thirty fasts or (stop when) we see the crescent. So I said: Is the sighting of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and his fasting not sufficient for you? He said: No, this is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us. And Yahya bin Yahya is in doubt whether the word in the hadith is ""naktafi"" or ""taktafi""."
"579","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two months of Eid are not deficient: one is Ramadan and the other is Dhul-Hijjah."
"580","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Partake in suhoor, for there is blessing in suhoor."
"581","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We took sahur with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stood up for the morning prayer. I (the narrator) asked: How much time was there between (sahur and the prayer)? He said: The time it takes to recite fifty verses. (The interval between finishing sahur and the call to prayer was about ten minutes.)"
"582","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not let Bilal’s (may Allah be pleased with him) call to prayer and the long whiteness in the sky deceive you regarding suhoor, until it spreads out like this. And (the narrator of the hadith) Hammad spread his hands out to the sides in this manner."
"583","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when this verse was revealed: “Eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread” { البقرہ : 178 } , a man who intended to fast would tie two threads to his foot, one white and the other black, and would continue eating and drinking until he could distinguish between the black and the white by looking at them. Then Allah the Exalted revealed the words “from the dawn,” and then people understood that by threads was meant the night and the day."
"584","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had two muezzins. One was Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) and the other was Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him), who was blind. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so keep eating and drinking until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer. The narrator said that there was not much time between the two calls to prayer, only as much as it took for one to descend and the other to ascend."
"585","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa and Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with them) say that in Ramadan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter the morning in a state of major ritual impurity due to intercourse, not a wet dream, and then he would fast."
"586","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked, while Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) was listening from behind the door. The man said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The time for prayer comes upon me while I am in a state of major impurity (junub), so should I fast?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “The time for prayer comes upon me as well while I am in a state of major impurity, then I fast.” The man said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You and we are not the same, because Allah Almighty has forgiven your past and future sins.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “By Allah, I hope that I am the most God-fearing among you and the most knowledgeable of those things from which one must abstain.” (So, the questioner thought that perhaps this ruling was specific to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) clarified that this ruling applies equally to him and to everyone. And from this hadith, it is understood that a servant can never be exempt from religious obligations and the requirements of servitude in any condition. And when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “I hope,” this is the perfection of servitude, otherwise, in reality, the rank of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is such that he is the most knowledgeable and God-fearing of all creation.)"
"587","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If a fasting person forgetfully eats or drinks, he should complete his fast, for it is Allah who has fed him and given him drink."
"588","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fasting person is invited to eat, he should say that I am fasting."
"589","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I am ruined."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""What has ruined you?"" He replied, ""I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Can you free a slave (male or female)?"" He said, ""No."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Can you fast for two consecutive months?"" He said, ""No."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Can you feed sixty poor people?"" He said, ""No."" (Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, says) Then he sat down until a basket of dates was brought to the Prophet (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Take this and give it as charity to the poor."" He said, ""Is there anyone poorer than me between the two black rocky plains of Madinah? In fact, there is no household in this area more in need than mine."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) laughed (may my parents be sacrificed for you, may I circle around you) until his blessed teeth became visible. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Take it and feed it to your family."
"590","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): She said that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""I am ruined."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Why?"" He said, ""I had intercourse with my wife during the day in Ramadan."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Give charity, give charity."" He said, ""I do not have anything."" Meanwhile, two baskets (of grain or dates) were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said, ""Take these and give them as charity."
"591","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), while in the state of fasting, would kiss (his wives) and embrace them (i.e., hold them close). But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had the greatest control over his desires among all of you."
"592","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on a journey in the month of Ramadan. When the sun had set, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O so-and-so! Dismount and mix sattu (barley drink) for us."" He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! It is still daytime."" (That is, this companion thought that when the redness after sunset disappears and night comes, then it is time, although this is incorrect.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) again said, ""Dismount (from the camel) and mix sattu for us."" Then he dismounted, mixed sattu, and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who drank it. Then he gestured with his hand and said, ""When the sun sets on this side (i.e., in the west) and night comes from this side (i.e., from the east), the fasting person should break his fast."
"593","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain upon goodness as long as they hasten in breaking the fast."
"594","It is narrated from Abu Atiyyah that he said: I and Masruq went to Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and Masruq said to her: O Umm al-Mu'minin! Among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), there are two persons who do not fall short in goodness and virtue. One of them breaks his fast at the earliest time and also prays at the earliest time, while the other delays both breaking the fast and the prayer. Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: Who is the one who breaks his fast early and prays at the earliest time? We said: He is Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him). Umm al-Mu'minin said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to do the same."
"595","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade continuous fasting (wisal), so a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You yourself observe wisal."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Which one of you is like me? I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."" Yet the people did not refrain from wisal (this was due to the perfect love and obedience of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, and they understood this prohibition as being out of compassion), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) observed wisal with them for one day, then for another day (he also observed wisal), then they saw the moon. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If the moon had not appeared, I would have continued wisal for longer."" (And the Prophet's saying this was by way of reprimand and rebuke, when they did not refrain from wisal.)"
"596","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled during Ramadan and observed the fast until he reached the place of Usfan. Then he (peace be upon him) asked for a bowl, in which there was something to drink, and he (peace be upon him) drank it during the day so that everyone could see. He continued to break the fast until he reached Mecca. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) both observed the fast and broke it, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break the fast."
"597","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out towards Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah during Ramadan and he was fasting, until he reached (the place) of Kura‘ al-Ghamim, and the people were also fasting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a cup of water, and he raised it until the people looked at him, then he drank it. (After that, the people also drank.) Then it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that some people were still fasting, so he said: ""They are the disobedient ones, they are the disobedient ones."
"598","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey when he saw a crowd of people around a man, and they were shading him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""What happened to him?"" The people replied, ""He is fasting."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""It is not righteousness to fast while traveling."
"599","`Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we fought in jihad with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the sixteenth of Ramadan, and some of us were fasting, and some had broken their fast (were not fasting), and the fasting person did not find fault with the one who had broken his fast, nor did the one who had broken his fast find fault with the fasting person."
"600","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey. Some of us were fasting and some were not. We halted at a place during intense heat. Among us, the one who had a sheet had the most shade, and there were some who were shielding themselves from the sun with their hands. All those who were fasting lay down at the place, and those who were not fasting stood up and set up tents and gave water to the camels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who broke their fast today have taken much reward."
"601","Qaza’ah says: I came to Abu Sa’id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and there was a crowd of people around him. When the crowd dispersed, I said to him, “I do not ask you about what these people were asking;” and I asked him about fasting during travel. He said: We traveled to Makkah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and we were fasting. Then we stopped at a certain place and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “You are now close to your enemy, and breaking the fast will give you more strength. So, permission was given to not fast.” Some of us fasted and some of us did not. Then we stopped at another place and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Tomorrow morning you will meet your enemy, and breaking the fast will give you more strength. So all of you should break your fast.” His statement this time was a definite command, so all of us broke our fast. After that (i.e., after confronting the enemy), we looked at our army and saw that we used to fast during travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"602","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hamzah bin Amr Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) that I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! I find myself strong enough to fast while traveling, so if I fast (during travel), is there any sin upon me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""It is a concession from Allah. So whoever takes it has done well, and whoever wishes to fast, there is no sin upon him."
"603","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during Ramadan in intense heat, to the extent that some of us would place our hands on our heads due to the severity of the heat, and none among us was fasting except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"604","Abu Salamah says: I heard from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: ""Whenever I had to make up missed fasts of Ramadan, I could not make them up except in Sha'ban, and the reason for this was that I used to be occupied in the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and would not find the opportunity."
"605","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies and has (missed) fasts to make up, his heir should fast on his behalf."
"606","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a woman came and said, ""I had given a slave girl in charity to my mother, and now my mother has passed away."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Your reward is established, and now that slave girl has come back to you due to inheritance."" She said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My mother had one month of (missed) fasts; should I fast on her behalf?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes, fast on her behalf."" She said, ""My mother had not performed Hajj; should I perform Hajj on her behalf?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Perform Hajj on her behalf as well."
"607","Narrated by Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him): When this verse was revealed, “And as for those who can fast with difficulty, they have (a choice either to fast or) to feed a poor person (for every day)” (Al-Baqarah: 184), whoever wished not to fast would leave the fast and give fidyah. Then the following verse was revealed, which abrogated it. (Meaning, if one has the ability, then he cannot break the fast and give fidyah instead.)"
"608","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Shaqiq (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I asked Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), “Did the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever fast for the entire days of any month?” She replied, “I do not know that he (peace be upon him) ever fasted the entire month except for Ramadan, nor did he ever leave fasting for an entire month. Rather, he (peace be upon him) used to fast some days in every month until he (peace be upon him) departed from this world (may Allah’s peace and mercy be upon him).”"
"609","`Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever fasts for one day in the way of Allah (jihad), Allah Almighty will keep his face seventy years' distance away from the Hellfire."
"610","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After the fasts of Ramadan, the most virtuous of all fasts are those of Muharram, which is the month of Allah, and after the obligatory prayers, the most virtuous prayer is the night (Tahajjud) prayer."
"611","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): The Quraysh used to fast on the day of Ashura (the 10th of Muharram) during the days of ignorance. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also commanded fasting on this (day), until Ramadan was made obligatory. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever wishes may fast on this day (Ashura), and whoever wishes may break the fast."
"612","It is narrated from Hakam bin A'raj, he said: I came to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), and he was sitting by the side of Zamzam, reclining on his cloak. So I said to him: Tell me about the fasting of 'Ashura. He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, keep counting the days. Then when it is the ninth (9th) day, fast on that day. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do the same? He said: Yes."
"613","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he saw that the Jews were fasting on the day of Ashura. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them, ""Why do you fast on this day?"" They said, ""This is a great day in which Allah Almighty saved Musa (peace be upon him) and the Children of Israel (from Pharaoh), and drowned Pharaoh and his people. Therefore, Musa (peace be upon him) fasted on this day out of gratitude, and we also fast."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""We are closer and have more right to Musa (peace be upon him) than you."" Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted on that day and ordered his Companions to fast as well."
"614","‘Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid narrates that he heard from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them). He was asked about fasting on the day of ‘Ashura, so he said: I do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fasted on any day, seeking the virtue of that day over other days, except this day, and of any month except the month of Ramadan (that is, among the days, he considered the day of ‘Ashura virtuous, and among the months, Ramadan)."
"615","Lady Rubayyi’ bint Mu’awwidh bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent an order on the morning of ‘Ashura to the settlements of the Ansar around Madinah that whoever has kept the fast should complete his fast, and whoever has eaten since morning should complete the rest of the day (i.e., should not eat anything now). After that, we used to fast and also made our small children fast as Allah willed, and we would go to the mosque and make cotton dolls for the children. Then, when any (child) cried for food, we would give him that (doll) to play with until the time of iftar came."
"616","Sayyiduna Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would fast so much that we would say he has fasted a lot, and he would refrain from fasting so much that we would say he has not fasted. And I did not see him fast in any month more than he fasted in Sha'ban. It was as if he fasted the entire month of Sha'ban. He would fast almost the whole of Sha'ban except for a few days."
"617","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him or to someone else: ""Did you fast any days at the beginning of Sha'ban?"" He replied, ""No."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""When you have broken your fast, then fast for two days."" (That is, when you have finished the month of Ramadan, then fast for two days.)"
"618","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts in Ramadan and then follows it with six days of fasting in Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted for the whole year."
"619","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasting during the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah."
"620","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked, ""How do you fast?"" At this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became angry (because this question was inappropriate; he should have asked, 'How should I fast?'). Then, when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw the Prophet's anger, he said, ""We are pleased with Allah as our Lord, with Islam as our religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) as our Prophet, and we seek refuge in Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) from anger."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) kept repeating these words until the Prophet's anger subsided. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What about the one who fasts every day?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""He neither fasted nor broke his fast."" Then he asked, ""What about the one who fasts two days and breaks his fast one day?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Who has the strength for that?"" Then he asked, ""What about the one who fasts one day and breaks his fast one day?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This is the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him)."" Then he asked, ""What about the one who fasts one day and breaks his fast two days?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I wish I had the strength for that (meaning, this is also good if one has the strength)."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Three fasts every month and the fasts of Ramadan, from one Ramadan to the next, this is like perpetual fasting (in reward)."" And the fast of the day of Arafah, I hope from Allah that it will be an expiation for the sins of the previous year and the coming year, and from the fast of Ashura, I hope it will be an expiation for the previous year."
"621","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Fadl bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) that some people came to her and differed about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Arafah (in Arafat). Some said that he was fasting and others said that he was not. Then Umm Fadl sent a bowl of milk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was staying on his camel in Arafat, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) drank it."
"622","Abu Ubaid, the freed slave of Ibn Azhar, narrates that I attended Eid with Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He came and performed the prayer. Then, after finishing, he delivered a sermon to the people and said: ""These two days are such that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on them. One is the day of your breaking the fast after Ramadan, and the other is the day on which you eat from your sacrifices."
"623","`Sayyiduna Nubaisha Hudhali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The days of Tashreeq (the 11th, 12th, and 13th of Dhul-Hijjah) are days of eating and drinking. And in another narration: ... and of remembering Allah (with the meat)."
"624","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about fasting on Monday. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On this day I was born and on this day revelation was sent down to me."
"625","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No person should fast specifically on Friday, unless he fasts a day before it or a day after it as well."
"626","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: No person should single out the night of Jumu'ah (Friday) among all nights for standing (in prayer) and nor its day (i.e., Friday) among all days for fasting, unless it is his regular practice (such as fasting on a specific date every month) and Jumu'ah happens to fall on that day."
"627","It is narrated from Sayyida Mu'adhah al-'Adawiyyah that she asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to fast three days every month. She replied, ""Yes."" Then she asked, ""On which days did he fast?"" She said, ""He did not mind; he would fast on any day."
"628","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin As (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` news reached the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I observe fasts continuously (without break) and spend the whole night in prayer. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent someone to me or I met him myself, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been informed that you observe fasts continuously without breaking them and spend the whole night in prayer. Do not do so. For your eyes have a right over you, your own self has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. So observe fasts and also break them, and offer (voluntary) prayers and also sleep. And fast one day in every ten days, for you will get the reward of (fasting) the remaining nine days as well. I said: I find in myself the strength for more than this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then observe the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him). I said: O Noble Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What was his fast? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He would fast one day and break the fast the next day, and when he faced the enemy, he would never flee (from jihad). Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Noble Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! How can I attain this not fleeing from the enemy (i.e., this is a matter of great strength and bravery). Ata (the narrator of the hadith) said: Then I do not know how the mention of perpetual fasting came, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding this: Whoever fasted perpetually did not fast at all (i.e., did not attain the complete reward). Whoever fasted perpetually did not fast at all."
"629","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The most beloved fast to Allah is the fast of Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him), and the most beloved prayer is the prayer of Dawud (peace be upon him). (Sayyiduna Dawud [peace be upon him]) used to sleep half the night, stand (in prayer) for one third of it (i.e., perform Tahajjud), and then sleep for one sixth of it. And he used to fast one day and break his fast the next day."
"630","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that one day the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me and said, “Do you have anything (to eat)?” We said, “There is nothing.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Then I am fasting.” Then on another day the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! We have received hais as a gift.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Show it to me, and I was fasting since morning.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ate."
